{"type": "message", "id": "a2d88185", "parentId": "cbdcf2dc", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T16:05:51.098Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_cd2021b1d602473fb9165fdb", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"grade 8 math score 2022 Nation's Report Card average score 270\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 994,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3cd2511fb031fb33\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3cd2511fb031fb33\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e786be4009308466\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBL<strong>IC)</strong>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e786be4009308466\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f985bf03d05f2de2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f985bf03d05f2de2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58feef2b00666c0f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58feef2b00666c0f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddd0121049368b17\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddd0121049368b17\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f04d1cbfdd87c9c3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f04d1cbfdd87c9c3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"62090f84e10a7ffc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ALASKA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"62090f84e10a7ffc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://education.alaska.gov/assessments/snapshot_MAT2022AK_8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d68f3129af6f7bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>In 2022, the average score of eighth-grade students in Alaska was 270</strong>. This was · lower than the average score of 273 for students in the nation. ... * Significantly different (p &lt; .05) from state&#x27;s results in 2022. Significance tests were performed using ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d68f3129af6f7bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"education.alaska.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6dc864a7f4fca50\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6dc864a7f4fca50\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"16e15f3cb92b3fd5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStudents also answered survey questions asking about their opportunities to learn about and engage in mathematics inside and outside of school. ... In 2022, average mathematics scores for the nation were lower by 5 points at fourth grade and <strong>lower by 8 points</strong> at eighth grade compared to scores ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"16e15f3cb92b3fd5\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b9ae0d35a3ce4ebe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAnalysis of 2022 NAEP Mathematics and Reading Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b9ae0d35a3ce4ebe\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://whiteboardadvisors.com/analysis-of-2022-naep-mathematics-and-reading-results/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b60c2f0dea6f1fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAverage eighth grade math score fell from 282 in 2019 to <strong>274</strong> in 2022 – a decline of 8 points\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b60c2f0dea6f1fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 24, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"whiteboardadvisors.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fafddce367a902d0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Nation's Report Card | NAEP\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fafddce367a902d0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ec3b0217dac8c0b8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP is an educational assessment. Often called The Nation&#x27;s Report Card, it provides national, state, and district-level results about students&#x27; academic achievement.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ec3b0217dac8c0b8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 9, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"04f595db3d85674b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"04f595db3d85674b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bd9a0282653d60e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile <strong>average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally</strong>, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bd9a0282653d60e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0686da46f559f8e3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n10 Takeaways from the 2024 NAEP Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0686da46f559f8e3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nagb.gov/powered-by-naep/the-2024-nations-report-card/10-takeaways-from-2024-naep-results.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d20c9e323d8e426d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn reading, Hispanic students are down 5 points; in math <strong>3 points</strong>. In 4th grade math, Black students, Hispanic students, and White students all saw average score gains, but this was driven by higher-performing students.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d20c9e323d8e426d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nagb.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4e03c7e5f7d381ea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4e03c7e5f7d381ea\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5f42f67a25e424d4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5f42f67a25e424d4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "grade 8 math score 2022 Nation's Report Card average score 270", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 994, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3cd2511fb031fb33\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3cd2511fb031fb33\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e786be4009308466\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBL<strong>IC)</strong>\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e786be4009308466\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f985bf03d05f2