le fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d797fb0bd9000141\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3d28c89ac3e9e95f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ALASKA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3d28c89ac3e9e95f\">>>", "url": "https://education.alaska.gov/assessments/snapshot_MAT2022AK_8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9072b0902b504101\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn 2022, <strong>the average score of eighth-grade students in Alaska was 270</strong>. This was · lower than the average score of 273 for students in the nation. ... * Significantly different (p &lt; .05) from state&#x27;s results in 2022. Significance tests were performed using ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9072b0902b504101\">>>", "siteName": "education.alaska.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a7dde0cbd03f5150\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a7dde0cbd03f5150\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0ff490edf92b5514\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0ff490edf92b5514\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e72846d14cc296ac\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe Nation's Report Card | NAEP\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e72846d14cc296ac\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6f88f2f9bc939189\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExplore NAEP results about student performance, and access state and district results, the NAEP data explorer, assessment items, item maps, and more.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6f88f2f9bc939189\">>>", "published": "February 9, 2026", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6416cd04f92d810e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAverage National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) mathematics scale score of 8th-grade public school students, by race/ethnicity, parents' highest level of education, and state or jurisdiction: 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6416cd04f92d810e\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/programs/digest/d23/tables/dt23_222.70.asp", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba998e3e22d9de12\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nPrevious Page Download Excel (38KB)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba998e3e22d9de12\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776355597229}}
